std::vector<int> exclusiveTime(int n, std::vector<std::string> logs) {
    std::vector<int> res(n, 0);
    std::vector<int> stack;
    int prev_time = 0;

    for (const auto& log : logs) {
        std::istringstream iss(log);
        std::string id_str, type, time_str;
        std::getline(iss, id_str, ':');
        std::getline(iss, type, ':');
        std::getline(iss, time_str, ':');

        int id = std::stoi(id_str);
        int time = std::stoi(time_str);

        if (type == "start") {
            if (!stack.empty()) {
                res[stack.back()] += time - prev_time;
            }
            stack.push_back(id);
            prev_time = time;
        } else {
            res[stack.back()] += time - prev_time + 1;
            prev_time = time + 1;
            stack.pop_back();
        }
    }

    return res;
}
```

### Explanation:
- The input `logs` is processed line by line.
- Each log entry is split into `id`, `type`, and `time`.
- If the type is "start", the current function's execution time is calculated and added to the result array for the corresponding function ID. Then, the ID is pushed onto the stack, and `prev_time` is updated.
- If the type is "end", the execution time of the function at the top of the stack is calculated, and `prev_time` is updated accordingly. The ID is then popped from the stack.
- This process continues until all logs have been processed, and the final result is returned.

